  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Efficiency, climate change and disaster resiliency, and sustainability of safe water and sanitation improved in Chuuk State</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2028:

At least 6,200 people, including at least 3,050 women, have access to continuous piped water supply system
(2020 baseline: 2,300 people, 1,150 women)
(OP 4.1) 
Achievement: 4112 
Progress/Status: As of July 2025, 596 households (serving approximately 4,112 people) have been connected to the CPUC water supply network on Weno (source: Project Review Mission in October 2025). 
Data Source: a.-d. Government statistical yearbooks; ADB mission reports, quarterly project progress reports, and project completion report; CPUC annual report; and gender-focused time-saving surveys</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="2300" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2028-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2028-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3050"></target>
     <actual value="4112"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">At least 4,650 people, including at least 2,300 women, are connected to the Weno sewerage system (2020 baseline: 2,400 people, 1,150 women) 
Achievement: 4375 
Progress/Status: As of July 2025, 634 households (serving approximately 4,112 people) have access to a mix of onsite sanitation facilities and sewerage system in Weno and Tonoas (source: Project Review Mission in October 2025) 
Data Source: a.-d. Government statistical yearbooks; ADB mission reports, quarterly project progress reports, and project completion report; CPUC annual report; and gender-focused time-saving surveys</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="2400" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2028-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2028-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="4650"></target>
     <actual value="4375"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 2</narrative>
